0000                   2  ; LINECFG          ADM-31 plugin ROM ($E000-$E7FF), >
0000                   3  ;
0000                   4  ; "ADMENU" -- lettered direct-command line configura>
0000                   5  ; Mickey's own sketch. Each letter performs its acti>
0000                   6  ; (sends the real ESC sequence, or updates internal >
0000                   7  ; redraws, rather than staging changes behind a sepa>
0000                   8  ;
0000                   9  ; What's real vs. stubbed, honestly:
0000                  10  ;   A/B (conversation/block), C/D (half/full duplex)>
0000                  11  ;   prefix) -- confirmed: sent as real ESC sequences>
0000                  12  ;   firmware's own processor via the traced zero-pag>
0000                  13  ;   E/F/G (parity/data bits/stop bits) -- confirmed >
0000                  14  ;   independent: the MC6850 ACIA at $7A00 packs all >
0000                  15  ;   3-bit word-select field with exactly 8 valid com>
0000                  16  ;   "7 data bits, no parity" exists on this chip). E>
0000                  17  ;   through that same shared set; changing one can v>
0000                  18  ;   other two on screen, because on the real hardwar>
0000                  19  ;   H (baud rate) -- NOT implemented. Tracing the AC>
0000                  20  ;   just now showed the counter-divide bits (the one>
0000                  21  ;   select baud) are hardcoded by stock firmware, no>
0000                  22  ;   software-selected at all -- baud is very likely >
0000                  23  ;   clock source this ROM has no path to control. Me>
0000                  24  ;   marked "N/A" rather than faked.
0000                  25  ;   I (local echo) -- stub. Likely a stock-firmware >
0000                  26  ;   location hasn't been traced.
0000                  27  ;   K (execute polling/opt ROM) -- stub. Would need >
0000                  28  ;   terminal's own polling-mode entry sequence works>
0000                  29  ;   L (show settings) -- shows this ROM's own tracke>
0000                  30  ;   live readback of stock firmware's internal state>
0000                  31  ;   M (reset to defaults) -- resets tracked state an>
0000                  32  ;   default ESC sequences.
0000                  33  ;   Q added (not in the original sketch): quit witho>
0000                  34  ;   anything further, straight back to normal termin>
0000                  35  ;
0000                  36  ; ==================================================>
0000                  37  ; HARDWARE I/O
0000                  38  ; ==================================================>
0000  =7000           39  HALT            EQU     $7000
0000  =7800           40  PIA1            EQU     $7800
